1
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,785
<i>NARRATOR: 
Five thousand years ago,</i>

2
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:39,038
<i>a fierce warrior 
known as the Scorpion King</i>

3
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,166
<i>led a great army on a campaign</i>

4
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:43,376
<i>to conquer the known world.</i>

5
00:00:51,843 --> 00:00:53,511
(ALL SHOUTING)

6
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,939
(SPEAKING IN 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

7
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,910
(SHOUTING)

8
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:09,295
<i>NARRATOR: 
After a vicious campaign 
which lasted seven long years,</i>

9
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:12,423
<i>the Scorpion King and his army 
were defeated</i>

10
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:16,177
<i>and driven deep 
into the sacred desert 
of Ahm Shere.</i>

11
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:31,192
(BIRD SCREECHING)

12
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:42,912
<i>One by one, 
they slowly perished 
under the scorching sun</i>

13
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:49,002
<i>until only 
the great warrior himself 
was left alive.</i>

14
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:57,886
<i>Near death,</i>

15
00:02:57,969 --> 00:03:01,931
<i>the Scorpion King made a pact 
with the dark god Anubis</i>

16
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:04,809
<i>that if Anubis 
would spare his life</i>

17
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:07,270
<i>and let him conquer 
his enemies,</i>

18
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:09,814
<i>he would give him his soul.</i>

19
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:21,659
<i>Anubis accepted his offer 
and spared his life.</i>

20
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,890
(YELLING)

21
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:52,023
<i>Anubis gave the Scorpion King 
command of his army,</i>

22
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:53,483
(GROWLING)

23
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:59,113
<i>And like an evil flood, 
they washed away 
all that lay before them.</i>

24
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,408
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

25
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:13,920
<i>When his task was done, 
Anubis forced 
the Scorpion King</i>

26
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:16,214
<i>to serve him for all time.</i>

27
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,924
(GRUNTS)

28
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:27,141
<i>His army was returned 
to the sands 
from whence they came,</i>

29
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:28,768
(GROWLING)

30
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:35,066
<i>Where they wait, silently,</i>

31
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:37,318
<i>to be awakened once again.</i>

32
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,259
(MICE SQUEAKING)

33
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:08,474
(GUN COCKING)

34
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:02,987
(SNARLING)

35
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,454
(BOTH SCREAM)

36
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,208
Alex?

37
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:19,337
What were you thinking, 
a mummy had come back 
to life?

38
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:21,172
I'll tell you 
a story sometime.

39
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:23,758
What are you doing down here? 
I told you to wait for us 
up in the temple.

40
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:24,842
But, Dad, I saw... 
No "buts."

41
00:06:24,884 --> 00:06:25,968
It's dangerous down here, 
Alex.

42
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,679
But I saw your tattoo. 
You saw what?

43
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:31,849
On a wall by the entrance. 
There's a cartouche 
just like it.

44
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:36,187
With the pyramid and the eye 
and the two kings 
and everything.

45
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:38,606
Really? 
Yeah.

46
00:06:38,689 --> 00:06:41,609
Okay, well, 
I'll be up to take a look 
at that in a minute.

47
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:43,486
In the meantime, 
I want you to wait for us 
up there.

48
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,612
But... But...

49
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:48,116
No, pick up your stuff, 
and I'll see you up 
in the temple. Go.

50
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,954
Go on. 
And... 
And what shall I do?

51
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,498
I don't know. Surprise me.

52
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:58,292
Build a better mousetrap. 
Okay.

53
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:01,212
While your mother 
goes and desecrates 
another tomb.

54
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:10,680
(HISSING)

55
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,561
Go away.

56
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,646
(GASPS)

57
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,441
Those are poisonous, 
you know. 
Only if they bite you.

58
00:07:22,525 --> 00:07:25,111
What was all that about? 
Oh, nothing.

59
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:27,822
Alex wanted 
to show me something.

60
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,907
I swear,

61
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:32,451
the kid gets more and more 
like you every day.

62
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:36,914
What, 
you mean more attractive, 
sweet and devilishly charming?

63
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:39,250
No, he's driving me crazy.

64
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,460
Now, where were we?

65
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,213
Hammer and chisel.

66
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:52,638
All right, all right! 
Let's do it your way. 
Thank you.

67
00:07:55,892 --> 00:07:57,643
(THUDDING)

68
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:16,954
Ever since I had that dream, 
this place is 
all I can think about.

69
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:21,292
Ever since you had that dream, 
I haven't had a decent night 
of sleep.

70
00:08:21,792 --> 00:08:24,253
EVELYN: I feel like 
I've been here before.

71
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:28,341
I know I've been here before. 
Evy, 
nobody's been here before.

72
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:31,677
Not in at least 3,000 years. 
Except for these guys.

73
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:39,477
Then how do I seem to know 
exactly where I'm going?

74
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,493
MAN: Let's go.

75
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,498
(MICE SQUEAKING)

76
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:13,970
(VOICES ECHOING)

77
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:33,072
Knock, knock. Anybody home?

78
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:39,328
You two check out that stuff, 
see if it's there.

79
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,831
I'll sort out the O'Connells.

80
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:18,094
You know, if you move that 
fast enough, you can almost 
write your name.

81
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,970
I just had a vision.

82
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:24,558
It was... 
It was like my dream, 
but it was real.

83
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:27,019
It was like 
I was actually here 
in ancient times.

84
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:31,649
Well, if you actually 
were here, could you show me 
how to open this thing?

85
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:33,651
Hold this.

86
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:52,753
All right, now you're 
starting to scare me. 
Now I'm starting 
to scare myself.

87
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:56,590
What is this? 
Look at the state 
of this rubbish.

88
00:11:56,674 --> 00:12:00,428
Those Egyptians 
never had a clue. 
It's all chintz and stuff.

89
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,346
Look at that.

90
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:06,559
Cheap pottery, this. 
Ancient rubbish.

91
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:07,977
(SCREAMING)

92
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:09,228
(GUN COCKING)

93
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:15,025
Jacques, 
something's hit me head! 
Shut up, Spivey. 
This place is cursed.

94
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,239
We do not want 
to wake the gods.

95
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:36,172
(GROANING)

96
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:45,014
EVELYN: That's the emblem 
of the Scorpion King.

97
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:47,224
He's supposed to be pure myth.

98
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:50,019
No... No trace of him 
has ever been found before.

99
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:53,063
No artifacts, 
no archival evidence.

100
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,065
Maybe they didn't want 
anybody to find him.

101
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:56,150
Let's open this.

102
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:58,944
Evy, I don't have 
a real good feeling 
about this.

103
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:02,406
It's only a chest. 
No harm ever came 
from opening a chest.

104
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:04,909
Right, 
and no harm ever came 
from reading a book.

105
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,578
Remember how that went? 
We can't stop now.

106
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,247
Just remember, 
I was the voice 
of reason here.

107
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:11,415
For once.

108
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:15,795
Rubbish. Rubbish. 
Dreck. Chintz.

109
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:17,755
Only half of this...

110
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,298
(GROANING)

111
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,760
(LAUGHING) 
God, that hurt!

112
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:45,658
Hon? Let's do it your way.

113
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:05,886
The bracelet of Anubis.

114
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:16,105
I'll take care of this.

115
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:19,066
(GUN COCKING)

116
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:20,859
(RUMBLING)

117
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,154
Oh, my God.

118
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:27,324
It's a bit late for that!

119
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:30,494
Put it in your rucksack. 
I got a better idea. 
Let's leave it here.

120
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:33,080
I think 
it's a bit late for that! 
What's it say?

121
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:38,502
"He who disturbs this bracelet 
shall drink from the Nile."

122
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,129
That doesn't sound too bad.

123
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:43,173
(SCREAMING)

124
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:02,776
Jacques's gonna make 
a nice fillet out of you, 
my son.

125
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:07,197
Oh, please. Please. 
Spivey! Jacques!

126
00:15:07,531 --> 00:15:10,701
Let's get the hell 
out of here! 
Come on!

127
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,500
Come on!

128
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:29,887
(GRUNTS)

129
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,060
(SCREAMS)

130
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,271
(BOTH SCREAMING)

131
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,358
(GRUNTING)

132
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,254
Whoa.

133
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:31,949
(BOTH SCREAMING)

134
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,044
(BOTH COUGHING)

135
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:48,424
Mom, Dad, 
I can explain everything.

136
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:19,079
<i>The Book of the Dead</i> 
gives life.

137
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,999
And <i>The Book of the Living</i>

138
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,295
takes life away.

139
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:28,964
I thought that was my job.

140
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:33,302
We're getting close.

141
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,305
(MEN CHATTERING)

142
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:04,833
Did you acquire it?

143
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:07,252
(RUMBLING)

144
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:25,729
(HORSE WHINNYING)

145
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:47,251
(SKITTERING)

146
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:49,711
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

147
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:00,430
We're getting very close.

148
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:07,146
(SKITTERING)

149
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,822
We've found him.

150
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:21,618
We've found him! 
We've found him!

151
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:41,179
Step aside here. 
Out of the way!

152
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:50,314
Imhotep. It's him. 
It's Imhotep.

153
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:57,196
Now we must raise 
those that serve him.

154
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:58,447
(MAN 1 SPEAKING ARABIC) 
MAN 2: Get out of my way.

155
00:19:58,488 --> 00:20:02,242
Get out of my way, 
or I'm gonna shoot you 
in the face.

156
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,828
He means it. 
He shot someone before.

157
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:09,583
Give it to me. 
The opportunity passed us by.

158
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,336
We need that bracelet.

159
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:14,963
And we need it 
before it opens.

160
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,469
Enough.

161
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:27,768
My dear Hafez, 
I told you I should have 
handled it.

162
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:32,147
I did not want 
your past history 
to cloud the issue.

163
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,858
We know where it is. 
We'll take care of it.

164
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,069
No, we'll take care of it.

165
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:40,447
I have a different chore 
for you now.

166
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:44,409
Where is the bracelet? 
It's on its way 
to merry old London.

167
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:48,372
Then London 
is where we must go.

168
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:08,100
The last known expedition 
to actually

169
00:21:08,141 --> 00:21:11,270
reach Ahm Shere 
was sent by Ramses IV

170
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,146
over 3,000 years ago.

171
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,941
He sent over a thousand men. 
And none of them 
was ever seen again.

172
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:18,068
How did you know? 
I didn't. 
But that's always the story.

173
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,570
Did I mention 
there was a pyramid of gold? 
Twice.

174
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:22,990
Alexander the Great 
sent troops in search of it.

175
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,783
Hooray for him. 
So did Caesar.

176
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,952
Yeah, look what happened 
to his career. 
And Napoleon.

177
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:30,289
But we're smarter than him. 
And taller, too.

178
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:34,126
Exactly. That's why 
we're gonna find it. 
Because we're taller?

179
00:21:35,293 --> 00:21:38,255
That's why I love you. 
Nice try.

180
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,300
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

181
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:00,527
ALEX: Mom!

182
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:02,779
What do I do with this chest?

183
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:05,032
This sucker weighs 
a goddang ton.

184
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:07,200
Alex, watch your language!

185
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:09,119
Rather weighty, this.

186
00:22:13,206 --> 00:22:14,416
(CLICKING)

187
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:15,834
Huh?

188
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:22,674
Evy, that first weird dream 
of yours was exactly 
six weeks ago, right?

189
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:25,886
I think so, yes. 
But what's that got to do 
with anything?

190
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:29,931
It just happens to coincide 
with Egyptian New Year.

191
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:33,727
Oh. That's right. 
What a coincidence.

192
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:39,649
Maybe. All I'm saying is, 
let's be cautious.

193
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:45,906
Oh!

194
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:52,120
If anything happened to you, 
I would never forgive myself.

195
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,085
(GASPS)

196
00:22:58,377 --> 00:22:59,795
(SNARLING)

197
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:14,976
You and Alex 
are the only thing 
that matter to me.

198
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,478
Well,

199
00:23:17,687 --> 00:23:21,233
the Bembridge scholars 
have been begging me

200
00:23:21,274 --> 00:23:23,318
to run the British Museum.

201
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:33,995
Wh... Whoa.

202
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:43,713
Hey, Alex, 
behave yourself 
for five minutes.

203
00:23:44,297 --> 00:23:45,715
You betcha.

204
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:57,477
Happy to be home? 
Couldn't be happier.

205
00:23:58,311 --> 00:24:00,689
It's the year of the scorpion.

206
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:02,941
Neat! 
Thought you might like that.

207
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:07,112
So then I killed the mummy 
and all his minions 
and stole his scepter.

208
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:11,074
Oh, you're so brave. 
And rich. 
Did I mention rich?

209
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:13,243
What do you think 
I'm doing here?

210
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,622
Sorry. We must be 
in the wrong house.

211
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:20,375
You said 
this was your house. 
No, I didn't.

212
00:24:20,458 --> 00:24:22,127
Call me!

213
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:25,589
You're not Sheila's husband, 
are you? 
No.

214
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:28,758
Look, if you work for Johnny, 
I was gonna pay him back 
on Tuesday.

215
00:24:28,842 --> 00:24:30,927
I don't know any Johnny.

216
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:33,305
We are looking 
for the bracelet of Anubis.

217
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:36,766
Oh, good for you. 
Good thing to have, 
the old bracelet of Anubis.

218
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:38,393
Where is it?

219
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:41,021
You're looking here 
for the bracelet. I see.

220
00:24:41,104 --> 00:24:43,106
I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

221
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:46,735
Mr. O'Connell, 
you try my patience.

222
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:50,030
Mr. O'Connell? 
No, hold on a minute. 
You've got the wrong...

223
00:24:50,113 --> 00:24:52,324
That bracelet. 
Now I remember.

224
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:56,036
I lost it in a card game. 
For your sake, I hope not.

225
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:01,500
It can't be.

226
00:25:02,542 --> 00:25:04,211
ANCK-SU-NAMUN: Hello.

227
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:08,757
Hello.

228
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:13,220
Where's your wife? 
My wife? Oh, you mean Evy.

229
00:25:13,303 --> 00:25:16,848
I think she went off 
to Baden-Baden 
or Tibet or something.

230
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:18,391
The girl's a free spirit.

231
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,769
Did I mention 
I was single now?

232
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,483
(HISSING)

233
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:29,444
Egyptian asps 
are quite poisonous.

234
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:31,947
It's downstairs. 
There's a safe.

235
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:36,576
The combination is 320-58...

236
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,787
393-something.

237
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:42,082
It's in a safe downstairs. 
I told you. I told you!

238
00:25:42,165 --> 00:25:43,375
And your point is?

239
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:45,710
My point is, 
I told you so you 
wouldn't kill me.

240
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:48,255
When did we make 
that arrangement?

241
00:25:52,425 --> 00:25:53,677
Hello.

242
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:58,640
Alex, I'm serious. 
If you've lost that key, 
you're grounded.

243
00:25:58,682 --> 00:26:01,685
I haven't lost it. 
I just can't find it. 
There's a difference.

244
00:26:01,726 --> 00:26:04,521
Well, you'd better start 
finding it then.

245
00:26:04,604 --> 00:26:06,982
I will, Mom. 
There's nothing 
to worry about.

246
00:26:07,023 --> 00:26:08,525
Good evening.

247
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:15,031
Who are you? 
What are you doing here?

248
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:17,784
I'm looking for the chest, 
of course.

249
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:21,454
Give it to me now.

250
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:29,170
Definitely not 
the best idea.

251
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:31,006
I think it's time to yell 
for Dad now.

252
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:34,676
Now I will kill you 
and take it anyway. 
ARDETH: I think not.

253
00:26:36,886 --> 00:26:39,848
Ardeth, 
what are you doing here?

254
00:26:39,889 --> 00:26:41,933
Perhaps explanations 
are best kept for later.

255
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:43,601
Ardeth Bay.

256
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:45,395
Lock-Nah.

257
00:26:46,604 --> 00:26:47,731
Knowing my brother-in-law,

258
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:49,858
he probably deserves 
whatever you're about 
to do to him,

259
00:26:49,899 --> 00:26:53,987
but this is my house, 
I have certain rules about 
snakes and dismemberment.

260
00:26:57,741 --> 00:26:58,992
Shoot him!

261
00:27:00,577 --> 00:27:02,787
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

262
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:25,935
Whoa, Mom! 
When did you learn to do that?

263
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:27,604
I have no idea.

264
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:34,319
That I learned 
from your father.

265
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:39,115
I'll take that. 
Whoa!

266
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:51,044
Not bad for a Medjai.

267
00:27:57,926 --> 00:27:59,135
Let go!

268
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:11,648
What's in the chest? 
The bracelet of Anubis!

269
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:29,833
They must not 
get the bracelet! 
Get it and get out of here!

270
00:28:36,339 --> 00:28:37,882
Mom, look out!

271
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:40,051
Evelyn!

272
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:45,682
Mom!

273
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:13,084
Rick!

274
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:16,087
Evelyn! 
Look out, Rick!

275
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:28,391
Dad! Dad!

276
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:30,894
Are you all right? 
Yeah.

277
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:32,437
Yeah? Okay.

278
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:35,523
O'Connell.

279
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:40,028
What are you doing here? 
No, scratch that. 
I don't care.

280
00:29:40,069 --> 00:29:41,988
Who are those guys? 
Where are they taking my wife?

281
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:44,741
My friend, I'm not sure,

282
00:29:44,824 --> 00:29:48,745
but wherever this man is, 
your wife will surely be.

283
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:52,290
Hey, I know him.

284
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:55,251
He's the curator. 
He works at 
the British Museum.

285
00:29:55,335 --> 00:29:57,128
Are you sure? 
Believe him.

286
00:29:57,212 --> 00:29:59,923
He spends more time there 
than at home.

287
00:30:02,175 --> 00:30:04,761
You're here, 
the bad guys are here, 
Evy's been kidnapped.

288
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,763
Let me guess. 
Yes, they once again removed

289
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:07,972
the creature from his grave.

290
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:09,098
I don't mean 
to point fingers,

291
00:30:09,182 --> 00:30:11,434
but isn't it your job 
to make sure 
that doesn't happen?

292
00:30:11,518 --> 00:30:13,186
That woman who was with him, 
she knows things

293
00:30:13,269 --> 00:30:15,104
that no living person 
could possibly know.

294
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,398
She knew exactly 
where the creature 
was buried.

295
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:20,610
We were hoping she would 
lead us to the bracelet. 
She obviously did.

296
00:30:20,693 --> 00:30:22,195
And now they have it.

297
00:30:22,278 --> 00:30:24,697
I wouldn't get 
too nervous just yet.

298
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:28,034
Is that gold?

299
00:30:28,117 --> 00:30:30,203
When I stuck it on, 
I saw the pyramids at Giza.

300
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:33,122
Then, whoosh! 
Straight across 
the desert to Karnak.

301
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:35,041
By putting this on, 
you have started 
a chain reaction

302
00:30:35,124 --> 00:30:37,377
that could bring 
the next apocalypse.

303
00:30:37,752 --> 00:30:41,840
You, lighten up. 
You, big trouble. 
You, get in the car.

304
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:49,681
I am sorry 
if I alarmed your son,

305
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:52,809
but you must understand, 
now that the bracelet 
is on his wrist,

306
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:55,019
we have only seven days before 
the Scorpion King awakens.

307
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:01,442
Whomever can kill 
the Scorpion King

308
00:31:01,484 --> 00:31:03,403
can send his army back 
to the Underworld

309
00:31:03,444 --> 00:31:06,197
or use it to destroy mankind 
and rule the Earth.

310
00:31:06,281 --> 00:31:07,782
That's why 
they dug up Imhotep.

311
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:10,201
He's the only guy tough enough 
to take out the Scorpion King.

312
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,452
That is their plan.

313
00:31:24,090 --> 00:31:27,635
Alex, 
I've got a big job for you. 
Stay here and protect the car.

314
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:30,305
I can do that. 
Protect the car?

315
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:33,182
Just because I'm a kid 
doesn't mean I'm stupid.

316
00:31:33,266 --> 00:31:35,727
I know. 
Dad!

317
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:39,898
If you see anyone 
come out screaming, 
it's just me.

318
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:43,651
Maybe you should stay here 
and watch him. 
Yes, now you're talking.

319
00:31:47,864 --> 00:31:51,159
You want the shotgun? 
No, I prefer the Thompson.

320
00:31:57,790 --> 00:31:59,459
If I were to say to you,

321
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:03,671
I'm a stranger 
traveling from the east, 
seeking that which is lost...

322
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:06,507
Then I would reply 
that I am a stranger 
traveling from the west.

323
00:32:06,549 --> 00:32:10,011
It is I whom you seek. How... 
Then it is true.

324
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:12,513
You have the sacred mark. 
What, that?

325
00:32:12,555 --> 00:32:15,016
No, that got slapped on me 
in an orphanage in Cairo.

326
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:20,521
That mark means 
you're a protector of man, 
a warrior for God, a Medjai.

327
00:32:20,563 --> 00:32:22,649
(GUN COCKING) 
Sorry. 
You've got the wrong guy.

328
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:28,821
(PEOPLE CHANTING)

329
00:32:57,850 --> 00:33:00,895
(HAFEZ CHANTING 
IN ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

330
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:09,112
Mr. Hafez.

331
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,827
They found him.

332
00:33:37,265 --> 00:33:39,767
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

333
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:01,164
(ROARING)

334
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:19,432
(HAFEZ CHANTING 
IN ANCIENT EGYPTIAN LANGUAGE)

335
00:34:39,660 --> 00:34:40,953
(GROWLING)

336
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:52,799
Imhotep.

337
00:34:53,674 --> 00:34:56,260
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

338
00:35:03,351 --> 00:35:05,019
(LAUGHING)

339
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:06,687
(DOOR OPENING)

340
00:35:06,729 --> 00:35:07,939
(GASPS)

341
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:30,586
Do not be frightened.

342
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:32,171
I am not afraid.

343
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:35,258
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

344
00:36:01,742 --> 00:36:07,456
You know, a couple 
of years ago this would've 
seemed really strange to me.

345
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:15,756
Lord Imhotep 
will be much pleased.

346
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:27,059
Where is it?

347
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,770
Where is the bracelet?

348
00:36:30,813 --> 00:36:32,273
I think I know.

349
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:37,445
At the very top 
of the gold pyramid, 
there was a huge diamond.

350
00:36:37,528 --> 00:36:38,654
Huge? How huge?

351
00:36:38,738 --> 00:36:44,076
It was so big, 
it would reflect the sun 
and wink at distant travelers,

352
00:36:44,118 --> 00:36:46,495
beckoning them 
to their deaths.

353
00:36:47,955 --> 00:36:49,957
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

354
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,769
Get... No! Get off!

355
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:14,315
Oh, my God.

356
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:17,485
(SCREAMING)

357
00:37:19,278 --> 00:37:20,488
Rick!

358
00:37:20,780 --> 00:37:22,323
(GUNS FIRING)

359
00:37:31,123 --> 00:37:32,333
Meela!

360
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:29,307
Go, go, go, go!

361
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:47,366
Oh, no. 
Not these guys again.

362
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:52,079
(ALL GROWLING)

363
00:38:59,712 --> 00:39:03,549
Honey, what you doing? 
These guys don't use doors.

364
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:08,220
Where the hell's Jonathan?

365
00:39:13,809 --> 00:39:15,561
Alex! 
What's the matter 
with my car?

366
00:39:15,644 --> 00:39:18,147
I was forced to find 
an alternative means 
of transportation.

367
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:20,566
A double-decker bus? 
It was his idea!

368
00:39:20,649 --> 00:39:21,859
Was not! 
Was too!

369
00:39:21,942 --> 00:39:22,943
Just go!

370
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:24,361
It was too! 
Was not!

371
00:39:24,403 --> 00:39:25,696
Oh, jeez.

372
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:42,046
No, no! Not my car!

373
00:39:46,467 --> 00:39:49,053
Oh, I hate mummies.

374
00:39:49,136 --> 00:39:52,014
Glad to see me now? 
Just like old times, huh?

375
00:40:11,575 --> 00:40:12,743
Right.

376
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:33,472
(SNARLING)

377
00:40:48,988 --> 00:40:50,364
(EXCLAIMS)

378
00:40:55,619 --> 00:40:56,871
(SNARLING)

379
00:40:58,497 --> 00:40:59,498
(SCREAMS)

380
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:13,971
(SNARLING)

381
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,352
(GRUNTING)

382
00:41:29,445 --> 00:41:30,446
(SNARLS)

383
00:41:31,614 --> 00:41:34,825
Turn! Turn! Turn! Turn! Turn!

384
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:38,287
(YELLING)

385
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:46,670
(GROWLING)

386
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:53,761
No! Get out of the way!

387
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:16,367
(SNARLING)

388
00:42:22,873 --> 00:42:24,416
ALEX: Look out!

389
00:42:30,839 --> 00:42:31,840
(GROWLING)

390
00:42:40,182 --> 00:42:41,517
(GRUNTING)

391
00:42:46,105 --> 00:42:48,691
(GLASS SHATTERING)

392
00:42:48,732 --> 00:42:50,150
Whoa!

393
00:43:23,350 --> 00:43:25,811
Great driving, Uncle Jon. 
Yeah.

394
00:43:32,901 --> 00:43:37,489
You all right? 
This was my first bus ride.

395
00:43:44,872 --> 00:43:46,373
What would I do without you?

396
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:50,502
Are all librarians 
this much trouble? 
Oh, jeez, get a room.

397
00:44:03,557 --> 00:44:05,392
Let me go! 
Alex!

398
00:44:05,434 --> 00:44:07,186
Silence! 
ALEX: Stop!

399
00:44:07,269 --> 00:44:09,772
Go! 
Stop!

400
00:44:14,109 --> 00:44:16,153
(BELL RINGING)

401
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:33,253
(GRUNTING)

402
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:43,972
Alex.

403
00:44:51,855 --> 00:44:53,941
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

404
00:44:56,985 --> 00:44:58,904
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

405
00:45:02,825 --> 00:45:04,785
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

406
00:45:54,376 --> 00:45:57,546
Please, do not fear 
for your son, my friends.

407
00:45:57,629 --> 00:46:01,300
They cannot hurt him, 
for he wears the bracelet 
of Anubis.

408
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,843
Alex is wearing 
the bracelet?

409
00:46:02,885 --> 00:46:06,388
When he put it on, he said 
he saw the pyramids at Giza, 
the temple at Karnak.

410
00:46:06,472 --> 00:46:11,143
And when they reach Karnak, 
the bracelet will show him 
the next step of the journey.

411
00:46:11,226 --> 00:46:12,561
Well, if we don't 
get to Karnak before them,

412
00:46:12,644 --> 00:46:15,314
we won't have any idea 
where to look for him next.

413
00:46:15,397 --> 00:46:19,234
Seems to me like 
we need a magic carpet.

414
00:46:19,568 --> 00:46:21,695
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

415
00:46:38,378 --> 00:46:40,964
When Lord Imhotep 
last encountered 
the O'Connells,

416
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:44,134
they sent his immortal soul 
to the Underworld.

417
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:48,305
As powerful as he will become, 
he is still vulnerable.

418
00:46:48,388 --> 00:46:52,100
Only with the Army of Anubis 
will he be invincible.

419
00:46:53,268 --> 00:46:55,229
He will need your help.

420
00:46:57,272 --> 00:46:58,941
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

421
00:46:58,982 --> 00:47:00,943
Keep this with you always.

422
00:47:02,110 --> 00:47:03,278
Hey!

423
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:05,155
<i>The Book of the Dead!</i>

424
00:47:05,239 --> 00:47:07,533
What a bright little child.

425
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:11,745
Your mother must be 
missing you terribly.

426
00:47:11,787 --> 00:47:14,540
If you wish to see her again, 
you'd better behave.

427
00:47:14,623 --> 00:47:17,042
Lady, I don't behave 
for my parents.

428
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:18,877
What makes you think 
I'm going to do it for you?

429
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:20,087
Silence!

430
00:47:20,128 --> 00:47:24,299
Because your parents 
wouldn't slip poisonous snakes 
into your bed

431
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:26,802
while you were sleeping.

432
00:47:27,511 --> 00:47:29,805
Lord Imhotep 
wishes to meet the boy.

433
00:47:30,681 --> 00:47:33,517
Now we shall see 
how brave you are.

434
00:47:34,518 --> 00:47:37,563
Hey! Watch the suit! Hey!

435
00:47:38,313 --> 00:47:39,856
Me fingers!

436
00:47:41,275 --> 00:47:42,442
Nice.

437
00:47:46,154 --> 00:47:47,698
Very nice.

438
00:47:47,781 --> 00:47:51,994
Did you acquire 
what we asked? 
Oh, we acquired it, all right.

439
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:53,745
You know what?

440
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:57,791
We had to kill 
two of those guards at 
the mausoleum to acquire it.

441
00:47:57,833 --> 00:47:59,876
This chest is cursed.

442
00:48:01,962 --> 00:48:08,218
It says there is one, 
the undead, who will kill 
all those who open this chest.

443
00:48:08,302 --> 00:48:10,178
Yes, yes, and the creature 
will suck them dry,

444
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:11,972
then become whole again.

445
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:13,890
We've all heard 
this story before.

446
00:48:13,974 --> 00:48:17,894
Yeah, but I heard the yanks 
who found it nine years ago 
all died.

447
00:48:17,978 --> 00:48:19,896
Horrible deaths, they were.

448
00:48:20,355 --> 00:48:22,858
So, with that in mind... 
We want ten.

449
00:48:22,899 --> 00:48:23,984
Quiet!

450
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:26,987
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

451
00:48:27,654 --> 00:48:29,406
The agreement was for five.

452
00:48:29,489 --> 00:48:32,200
Yeah, well, we want ten, 
or we'll take it elsewhere.

453
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:34,953
If you... 
Ten will be just fine.

454
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:36,747
Follow me, gentlemen.

455
00:48:38,707 --> 00:48:40,042
Get in.

456
00:48:46,423 --> 00:48:47,424
(GASPS)

457
00:48:55,891 --> 00:48:57,976
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

458
00:49:01,772 --> 00:49:04,733
It is you 
who are the chosen one,

459
00:49:04,775 --> 00:49:07,653
you who will take me 
to Ahm Shere.

460
00:49:07,736 --> 00:49:12,574
What if I don't? 
What if I get a little... lost?

461
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:14,868
(LAUGHING)

462
00:49:14,910 --> 00:49:17,537
You have strength, little one.

463
00:49:17,579 --> 00:49:19,748
You are your father's son.

464
00:49:19,831 --> 00:49:22,334
But I know something 
you don't.

465
00:49:22,417 --> 00:49:27,339
This bracelet is a gift 
and a curse.

466
00:49:27,964 --> 00:49:33,470
The sands of time 
have already begun 
to pour against you.

467
00:49:37,265 --> 00:49:39,351
Yeah, yeah. 
I already heard this part.

468
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:40,977
From the minute 
I put the bracelet on,

469
00:49:41,061 --> 00:49:43,897
seven days do I have before 
the Scorpion King wakes up.

470
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:46,608
Did you also hear 
that if you do not 
enter the pyramid

471
00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:49,194
before the sun strikes it 
on that very morning

472
00:49:49,277 --> 00:49:52,280
that the bracelet 
will suck the life out of you?

473
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:54,950
That part I missed.

474
00:49:54,991 --> 00:49:57,995
Hey, wait a minute. 
That means I've only got 
five days left.

475
00:49:58,078 --> 00:50:02,457
Then I believe 
it will be best if we do not 
get lost. Don't you?

476
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:05,752
My dad 
is going to kick your ass.

477
00:50:11,717 --> 00:50:13,093
(GASPS)

478
00:50:13,385 --> 00:50:15,429
I do not think so.

479
00:50:19,766 --> 00:50:23,854
In here, gentlemen, 
you shall receive 
your just rewards.

480
00:50:23,937 --> 00:50:25,856
No tricks now, woman.

481
00:50:26,231 --> 00:50:28,650
We're not giving up this chest 
till we're satisfied.

482
00:50:28,692 --> 00:50:32,571
Oh, don't worry. 
There is much satisfaction 
to be had.

483
00:50:32,779 --> 00:50:34,823
(WHOOSHING)

484
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:42,831
What's going on?

485
00:50:47,544 --> 00:50:51,173
This place is cursed.

486
00:50:51,256 --> 00:50:55,010
What is it with you 
and curses? 
He ain't happy 
without a curse.

487
00:50:55,093 --> 00:50:59,264
This is cursed. 
That is cursed. 
Give it a rest, will you!

488
00:50:59,723 --> 00:51:01,641
(ALL SCREAMING)

489
00:51:02,851 --> 00:51:04,144
Christ!

490
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:16,073
He wants you 
to open the chest! 
Open the chest!

491
00:51:16,782 --> 00:51:18,408
No!

492
00:51:36,676 --> 00:51:39,262
These are the commanders 
of the 12 tribes 
of the Medjai.

493
00:51:40,222 --> 00:51:41,473
Horus!

494
00:51:42,432 --> 00:51:43,892
(CHIRPING)

495
00:51:46,937 --> 00:51:50,357
Pet bird. 
My best 
and most clever friend.

496
00:51:50,774 --> 00:51:53,401
He will let the commanders 
know of our progress 
so that they may follow.

497
00:51:56,571 --> 00:51:58,949
Allah ma'ana (الله معنا)  "God is with us."

498
00:52:02,202 --> 00:52:04,371
(HORSES NEIGHING)

499
00:52:12,003 --> 00:52:14,297
If the Army of Anubis arises,

500
00:52:15,131 --> 00:52:17,759
they will do all they can 
to stop it.

501
00:52:18,093 --> 00:52:22,764
Rick, are you sure 
Izzy's reliable? 
Yeah, yeah, 
he's reliable-ish.

502
00:52:27,686 --> 00:52:30,689
Isn't she beautiful? 
It's a balloon.

503
00:52:30,772 --> 00:52:34,276
Oh! It's a dirigible. 
Where's your airplane?

504
00:52:34,317 --> 00:52:35,735
Airplanes are a thing 
of the past.

505
00:52:36,486 --> 00:52:39,239
Why can't you people 
ever keep your feet 
on the ground?

506
00:53:25,869 --> 00:53:29,789
O'Connell does not want 
to believe, but he flies like 
Horus towards his destiny.

507
00:53:29,873 --> 00:53:33,793
Yes, yes, very interesting. 
Tell me some more 
about this gold pyramid.

508
00:53:33,835 --> 00:53:36,504
Well, it is written 
that since the time 
of the Scorpion King,

509
00:53:36,588 --> 00:53:39,633
no man who has laid eyes 
upon it has ever returned 
to tell the tale.

510
00:53:39,716 --> 00:53:42,469
Where is all 
this stuff written? Hello.

511
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:45,639
Got it.

512
00:53:46,973 --> 00:53:48,516
(CHIRPING)

513
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:52,979
Pretty nice, eh?

514
00:53:53,355 --> 00:53:55,398
This is all I have left 
in the world.

515
00:53:55,482 --> 00:53:57,651
The rest of my fortune 
was lost

516
00:53:57,734 --> 00:54:00,320
to some rather 
unscrupulous characters, 
actually.

517
00:54:00,362 --> 00:54:03,782
But if the curator reacted 
to it the way you say, 
it must be very important.

518
00:54:03,823 --> 00:54:06,242
If I were you, 
I would keep it close.

519
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:09,329
My friend, 
the gods couldn't take this 
away from me.

520
00:54:09,412 --> 00:54:11,957
Hey! That's mine! 
No, it's not!

521
00:54:13,750 --> 00:54:15,835
Keep your hands off of it.

522
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:24,719
Hey.

523
00:54:25,804 --> 00:54:27,681
I want him back, Rick.

524
00:54:28,598 --> 00:54:31,226
I want him in my arms. 
I know.

525
00:54:34,062 --> 00:54:35,855
We taught him well.

526
00:54:37,065 --> 00:54:38,900
He's smarter than you

527
00:54:40,235 --> 00:54:41,987
and he's tougher than me.

528
00:54:42,070 --> 00:54:46,658
I love him so much. 
I just can't... 
I know. We both do, 
and Alex knows that.

529
00:54:48,576 --> 00:54:51,997
I'll get him back, Evy. 
I promise. 
I know you will.

530
00:55:19,399 --> 00:55:20,734
ALEX: Are we there yet? 
No.

531
00:55:20,817 --> 00:55:22,068
Are we there yet? 
No.

532
00:55:22,110 --> 00:55:23,236
Are we there yet? 
No.

533
00:55:23,278 --> 00:55:24,404
Are we there yet? 
No.

534
00:55:24,446 --> 00:55:25,572
Are we there yet? 
No.

535
00:55:25,613 --> 00:55:26,656
Are we there yet? 
No.

536
00:55:26,740 --> 00:55:27,741
Are we there yet? 
No.

537
00:55:27,824 --> 00:55:28,867
Are we there yet? 
No.

538
00:55:28,908 --> 00:55:30,118
Are we there yet? 
No.

539
00:55:30,201 --> 00:55:31,244
Are we there yet? 
No.

540
00:55:31,286 --> 00:55:32,912
Are we there yet? 
No.

541
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:35,749
Whoa! That was amazing!

542
00:55:35,832 --> 00:55:38,626
Perfect aim. 
What are you talking about?

543
00:55:40,128 --> 00:55:41,421
I missed.

544
00:55:49,846 --> 00:55:51,514
I have to go to the bathroom.

545
00:56:22,962 --> 00:56:24,506
Make it quick.

546
00:56:31,763 --> 00:56:33,014
Hurry up.

547
00:56:36,559 --> 00:56:39,062
Hey, reading material. 
Now!

548
00:56:43,858 --> 00:56:46,403
I can't go 
when someone's watching.

549
00:56:48,905 --> 00:56:50,490
I don't trust you. 
You'll look.

550
00:56:57,330 --> 00:56:59,541
(GRUNTING)

551
00:57:00,208 --> 00:57:01,417
Damn!

552
00:57:05,588 --> 00:57:09,676
Oh, my God! 
Doesn't anyone around here 
know how to flush a toilet?

553
00:57:28,528 --> 00:57:31,156
(WHEELS SCREECHING)

554
00:57:36,744 --> 00:57:38,538
(MEN CHATTERING)

555
00:57:42,750 --> 00:57:44,377
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

556
00:57:45,044 --> 00:57:46,963
(GUNS FIRING)

557
00:58:10,278 --> 00:58:11,529
Karnak.

558
00:58:24,083 --> 00:58:25,126
Huh?

559
00:58:46,522 --> 00:58:48,691
(CHIRPING)

560
00:58:52,445 --> 00:58:55,490
If a man does not 
embrace his past, 
he has no future.

561
00:58:55,573 --> 00:58:59,327
Look, even if

562
00:58:59,869 --> 00:59:03,581
I was some sort of 
sacred Medjai, what good 
does that do me now?

563
00:59:03,665 --> 00:59:05,792
It is the missing piece 
of your heart.

564
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:09,587
If you embrace it, 
if you accept it, 
you can do anything.

565
00:59:10,004 --> 00:59:11,839
Sounds great. Listen.

566
00:59:12,298 --> 00:59:15,301
What can we expect 
from our old friend Imhotep?

567
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:17,387
His powers are returning.

568
00:59:17,470 --> 00:59:18,596
By the time 
he reaches Ahm Shere,

569
00:59:18,638 --> 00:59:20,682
even the Scorpion King 
won't be able to stop him.

570
00:59:35,154 --> 00:59:39,117
<i>(IMHOTEP SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)</i>

571
01:00:09,731 --> 01:00:11,649
(MAN SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

572
01:00:43,514 --> 01:00:47,226
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

573
01:01:52,208 --> 01:01:54,293
(ALL CLAPPING)

574
01:02:09,142 --> 01:02:12,895
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

575
01:03:38,564 --> 01:03:40,483
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

576
01:03:41,901 --> 01:03:43,653
PHARAOH: Anck-su-namun!

577
01:03:56,415 --> 01:03:57,667
Imhotep!

578
01:03:58,834 --> 01:04:01,087
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

579
01:04:09,637 --> 01:04:11,472
(SCREAMING)

580
01:04:11,764 --> 01:04:12,890
Evy!

581
01:04:15,184 --> 01:04:16,185
(BOTH GRUNTING)

582
01:04:37,790 --> 01:04:39,041
Imhotep!

583
01:05:10,990 --> 01:05:13,492
Imhotep. 
Anck-su-namun.

584
01:05:21,292 --> 01:05:23,502
Evy, I know 
you haven't exactly 
been yourself lately

585
01:05:23,544 --> 01:05:25,171
with all these dreams 
and visions...

586
01:05:25,212 --> 01:05:27,757
No, no, 
they're memories 
from my previous life.

587
01:05:27,840 --> 01:05:30,718
Honestly, I'm not 
losing my mind. It all 
makes perfect sense now.

588
01:05:30,843 --> 01:05:32,678
And that's the reason 
why we found the bracelet?

589
01:05:32,762 --> 01:05:34,722
Exactly. I was its protector.

590
01:05:34,805 --> 01:05:36,349
Now do you believe, 
my friend?

591
01:05:36,390 --> 01:05:38,643
Clearly, you were destined 
to protect this woman.

592
01:05:38,684 --> 01:05:42,146
Right. 
She's a reincarnated princess, 
and I'm a warrior for God.

593
01:05:42,188 --> 01:05:46,400
And your son leads the way 
to Ahm Shere. 
Three sides of the pyramid.

594
01:05:46,525 --> 01:05:49,195
This was all preordained 
thousands of years ago.

595
01:05:49,278 --> 01:05:50,905
And how does the story end?

596
01:05:50,988 --> 01:05:54,075
Only the journey's written, 
not the destination.

597
01:05:54,158 --> 01:05:57,161
Convenient. 
How else do you explain 
Evy's visions?

598
01:05:57,203 --> 01:05:59,830
That it is your son 
who wears the bracelet?

599
01:05:59,872 --> 01:06:02,500
How do you explain your mark? 
Coincidence.

600
01:06:02,667 --> 01:06:07,088
My friend, 
there is a fine line between 
coincidence and fate.

601
01:06:27,316 --> 01:06:29,402
Don't even think about it!

602
01:06:33,155 --> 01:06:35,074
Hold on there, partner.

603
01:06:38,452 --> 01:06:40,246
When the time comes,

604
01:06:41,247 --> 01:06:43,624
I shall truly 
enjoy killing you.

605
01:06:45,584 --> 01:06:47,378
But until that time,

606
01:06:48,337 --> 01:06:50,881
you better be 
a little nicer to me.

607
01:06:51,215 --> 01:06:53,092
Now, where's my water?

608
01:06:57,096 --> 01:06:58,305
No ice?

609
01:07:01,017 --> 01:07:02,768
(SPEAKING 
ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

610
01:07:03,728 --> 01:07:05,771
Make sure he doesn't move!

611
01:07:36,051 --> 01:07:38,304
They've gone. We've lost them.

612
01:07:54,612 --> 01:07:55,696
Rick!

613
01:08:04,914 --> 01:08:06,707
Alex left us his tie,

614
01:08:07,333 --> 01:08:10,711
and he made us 
a little sand castle.

615
01:08:11,587 --> 01:08:13,672
It's the Temple Island 
of Philae.

616
01:08:13,714 --> 01:08:15,633
They've gone to Philae. 
That-a-boy, Alex.

617
01:08:15,674 --> 01:08:16,967
Come on!

618
01:08:28,687 --> 01:08:31,023
The great temple 
of Abu Simbel.

619
01:08:31,357 --> 01:08:33,025
(CHIRPING)

620
01:09:33,961 --> 01:09:36,881
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

621
01:09:58,444 --> 01:10:00,779
That's the Blue Nile 
down there.

622
01:10:00,905 --> 01:10:02,406
We must be 
out of Egypt by now.

623
01:10:02,448 --> 01:10:05,910
In ancient times, 
all this still belonged 
to the upper kingdom.

624
01:10:06,327 --> 01:10:08,537
The oasis must be 
around here somewhere.

625
01:10:08,621 --> 01:10:11,540
RICK: Don't worry, Evy, 
we'll find him. 
He's a smart kid.

626
01:10:11,624 --> 01:10:13,500
He'll leave us a sign.

627
01:10:18,714 --> 01:10:20,507
Surprised to see me?

628
01:10:21,175 --> 01:10:23,802
Leaving bread crumbs, 
huh? Huh?

629
01:10:24,136 --> 01:10:28,724
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

630
01:11:10,516 --> 01:11:11,517
(GASPS)

631
01:11:17,648 --> 01:11:20,109
We're in trouble!

632
01:11:21,110 --> 01:11:22,236
Whoa!

633
01:11:25,447 --> 01:11:26,782
(GROWLING)

634
01:11:32,413 --> 01:11:33,831
Horus, fly!

635
01:11:36,625 --> 01:11:40,713
Izzy, come hard right! 
Starboard! Starboard!

636
01:11:40,796 --> 01:11:42,423
(GRUNTING)

637
01:12:15,289 --> 01:12:18,042
(ALL PANTING)

638
01:12:23,881 --> 01:12:26,633
Was there a little something 
you forgot to mention?

639
01:12:31,388 --> 01:12:32,598
People?

640
01:12:40,522 --> 01:12:42,399
(BIRDS TWITTERING)

641
01:12:44,693 --> 01:12:47,029
(MONKEYS CHATTERING)

642
01:12:51,784 --> 01:12:53,118
Ahm Shere.

643
01:13:04,129 --> 01:13:05,339
Right.

644
01:13:05,422 --> 01:13:07,508
(RUMBLING)

645
01:13:12,304 --> 01:13:13,388
He's back!

646
01:13:13,514 --> 01:13:15,140
(GROWLING)

647
01:13:17,142 --> 01:13:18,435
Hang on!

648
01:13:32,241 --> 01:13:34,118
Well, that's not good.

649
01:13:35,661 --> 01:13:36,912
RICK: Hang on!

650
01:13:44,503 --> 01:13:45,587
Mom?

651
01:13:46,672 --> 01:13:47,756
Dad?

652
01:13:57,683 --> 01:13:59,184
RICK: 
We're gonna go get my son.

653
01:13:59,268 --> 01:14:00,894
Then we're gonna wanna 
get out of here fast,

654
01:14:00,978 --> 01:14:02,104
so make this work, Izzy.

655
01:14:06,692 --> 01:14:08,235
Come to Daddy.

656
01:14:10,195 --> 01:14:11,488
(WHISTLING)

657
01:14:11,572 --> 01:14:12,739
Horus!

658
01:14:12,823 --> 01:14:15,534
(CHIRPING)

659
01:14:21,540 --> 01:14:25,252
JONATHAN: So, Rick, 
what's the plan? 
RICK: Let's find 
some higher ground.

660
01:14:30,215 --> 01:14:33,093
(HORUS CHIRPING)

661
01:14:42,352 --> 01:14:43,812
(GUN FIRES)

662
01:14:44,563 --> 01:14:45,772
Horus!

663
01:14:52,362 --> 01:14:53,989
I must go. 
Where?

664
01:14:54,072 --> 01:14:55,616
I must let the commanders 
know where we are.

665
01:14:55,657 --> 01:14:57,534
You can't go. 
If the Army 
of Anubis arises...

666
01:14:57,618 --> 01:15:00,078
I need you 
to help me find my son.

667
01:15:05,459 --> 01:15:08,003
Then first, I shall help you. 
Thank you.

668
01:15:18,972 --> 01:15:20,933
(CRICKETS CHIRPING)

669
01:15:47,000 --> 01:15:49,336
Look. Roman legionnaires.

670
01:15:51,880 --> 01:15:55,676
And here. 
Turn-of-the-century French. 
Napoleon's troops.

671
01:15:55,759 --> 01:15:58,345
What in the name 
of Anubis did this?

672
01:16:06,353 --> 01:16:08,563
(GROWLING)

673
01:16:19,366 --> 01:16:21,201
You hear that? 
What?

674
01:16:22,577 --> 01:16:23,870
Nothing.

675
01:16:24,830 --> 01:16:26,581
Absolutely nothing.

676
01:16:31,044 --> 01:16:32,546
You any good with that?

677
01:16:32,796 --> 01:16:35,799
Three times Fox and Hound's 
grand champion, 
I'll have you know.

678
01:16:35,882 --> 01:16:39,344
You any good with that? 
You'll know soon enough.

679
01:16:43,890 --> 01:16:46,310
Evy, try to remember to...

680
01:16:47,978 --> 01:16:50,731
Just keep it tight 
in the shoulder and

681
01:16:52,649 --> 01:16:55,444
lead the target a little bit, 
and then...

682
01:16:56,612 --> 01:16:59,114
And squeeze the trigger. 
Don't pull it.

683
01:17:00,949 --> 01:17:02,451
I won't miss.

684
01:17:27,434 --> 01:17:29,561
(SNARLING)

685
01:17:42,199 --> 01:17:44,326
Pyramid. 
The pyramid.

686
01:17:45,035 --> 01:17:47,162
Cripes, I'm in trouble now.

687
01:17:47,537 --> 01:17:49,331
Now may I kill him?

688
01:17:49,956 --> 01:17:52,167
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

689
01:18:02,177 --> 01:18:04,638
Retrieve that bracelet. 
With pleasure.

690
01:18:18,068 --> 01:18:20,028
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

691
01:18:22,697 --> 01:18:24,741
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

692
01:18:30,956 --> 01:18:33,667
Something is coming.

693
01:18:47,222 --> 01:18:49,099
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

694
01:18:54,604 --> 01:18:56,189
Jonathan? 
Yes?

695
01:18:56,815 --> 01:18:59,568
That's my husband 
and my son down there.

696
01:18:59,901 --> 01:19:01,445
Make me proud.

697
01:19:02,446 --> 01:19:04,364
Today's that day, Evy.

698
01:19:04,740 --> 01:19:05,907
(GUN COCKING)

699
01:19:10,996 --> 01:19:12,414
(MAN SHOUTING IN ARABIC)

700
01:19:12,497 --> 01:19:14,082
Where's the boy?

701
01:20:18,730 --> 01:20:20,315
The black book!

702
01:20:25,320 --> 01:20:26,655
Let's go!

703
01:20:27,697 --> 01:20:30,158
(PEOPLE YELLING)

704
01:20:32,953 --> 01:20:34,621
(MEN SHOUTING)

705
01:20:56,268 --> 01:20:57,811
There you are!

706
01:20:57,853 --> 01:20:59,855
(GUNS FIRING)

707
01:21:00,397 --> 01:21:03,942
The time has come, 
my little friend. 
Let go!

708
01:21:17,455 --> 01:21:20,000
Dad! 
Alex!

709
01:21:21,459 --> 01:21:22,669
Alex...

710
01:21:30,093 --> 01:21:31,136
Dad!

711
01:21:40,645 --> 01:21:43,481
Time to remove that bracelet, 
my good son.

712
01:21:43,648 --> 01:21:44,733
Dad!

713
01:21:54,034 --> 01:21:56,578
Dad, behind you! 
Whoa!

714
01:22:02,375 --> 01:22:03,960
(YELLING)

715
01:22:12,761 --> 01:22:14,220
(MEN GRUNTING)

716
01:22:19,184 --> 01:22:20,852
(MEN EXCLAIMING)

717
01:22:26,566 --> 01:22:28,026
(SNARLING)

718
01:23:06,314 --> 01:23:07,857
(GUN FIRES)

719
01:23:19,786 --> 01:23:22,122
Let's go. 
Thank God for that.

720
01:23:29,295 --> 01:23:33,258
The two of you must 
sacrifice yourselves for me.

721
01:23:34,259 --> 01:23:36,636
You shall be rewarded 
in heaven!

722
01:23:42,767 --> 01:23:44,227
(SNARLING)

723
01:23:51,818 --> 01:23:53,236
Mom! 
Alex!

724
01:23:54,529 --> 01:23:55,613
Hey, nice shootin', Tex.

725
01:23:55,697 --> 01:23:57,824
What were those creepy 
little pygmy things?

726
01:23:57,907 --> 01:24:00,118
Just the local natives. 
Are you sure?

727
01:24:00,201 --> 01:24:01,453
I'm sure. It was nothin'.

728
01:24:01,536 --> 01:24:03,538
Come on, Mom! 
Come on! Come on, Dad!

729
01:24:03,621 --> 01:24:06,958
We have to get to the pyramid. 
I have to get the bracelet 
off now!

730
01:24:07,000 --> 01:24:09,044
Oh, leave it on, Alex. 
Looks good on you.

731
01:24:09,127 --> 01:24:11,129
No, you guys! 
You don't understand!

732
01:24:11,171 --> 01:24:12,881
He told me the bracelet 
will kill me

733
01:24:12,964 --> 01:24:15,800
if I don't get inside 
the pyramid 
before the sun hits it!

734
01:24:15,884 --> 01:24:18,428
Today! 
Oh, my God.

735
01:24:18,553 --> 01:24:20,722
(CREATURES SCREECHING)

736
01:24:22,140 --> 01:24:23,558
Time to go!

737
01:24:29,522 --> 01:24:31,149
(SCREECHING)

738
01:24:40,450 --> 01:24:43,411
JONATHAN: Wait for me! 
EVELYN: Hurry up, Jonathan!

739
01:24:44,662 --> 01:24:47,207
Wait for me! What's that for?

740
01:24:47,373 --> 01:24:49,876
Ah, nothin'. 
Just a little something 
in case of an emergency.

741
01:24:50,960 --> 01:24:52,378
(SCREECHING)

742
01:25:07,977 --> 01:25:09,103
Rick.

743
01:25:12,899 --> 01:25:14,484
Let's go, Alex!

744
01:25:23,618 --> 01:25:27,080
Run! Come on, Alex, 
faster! Come on!

745
01:25:27,455 --> 01:25:30,708
Come on! 
Dad! The bracelet!

746
01:25:30,875 --> 01:25:32,836
Run! Come on!

747
01:25:51,187 --> 01:25:52,730
(BOTH PANTING)

748
01:25:55,859 --> 01:25:58,361
You know, it's not

749
01:25:58,862 --> 01:26:00,864
easy being a dad.

750
01:26:02,282 --> 01:26:04,951
Yeah, 
but you do it really good.

751
01:26:06,286 --> 01:26:07,537
Thanks.

752
01:26:26,639 --> 01:26:29,142
They made it. Thank God.

753
01:26:30,226 --> 01:26:32,103
Oh, yes. Great.

754
01:26:32,812 --> 01:26:34,105
Fabulous.

755
01:26:35,148 --> 01:26:36,316
(GROANS)

756
01:26:37,692 --> 01:26:38,776
No!

757
01:26:51,623 --> 01:26:52,707
Evy!

758
01:26:53,166 --> 01:26:54,250
Evy!

759
01:26:59,672 --> 01:27:01,716
Jonathan! Jonathan! 
Mom!

760
01:27:03,009 --> 01:27:05,970
You're going to be all right. 
Isn't she, Dad? 
She'll be fine.

761
01:27:06,012 --> 01:27:08,723
She's going to be all right. 
Just get him... 
Take him. Take...

762
01:27:08,806 --> 01:27:10,767
Mommy's fine. It's okay.

763
01:27:12,018 --> 01:27:14,020
Where... Evy... 
Your mother's 
gonna be fine, okay?

764
01:27:14,062 --> 01:27:15,688
Oh, my God!

765
01:27:16,481 --> 01:27:19,192
You're real strong. 
You're gonna make it. 
You're gonna make it.

766
01:27:19,275 --> 01:27:20,693
RICK: You're fine.

767
01:27:21,236 --> 01:27:24,697
What do I do? 
What do I do, Evy?

768
01:27:25,365 --> 01:27:28,326
What do I do? 
Take care of Alex.

769
01:27:30,536 --> 01:27:33,873
No. Sweetheart, no.

770
01:27:36,209 --> 01:27:37,585
I love you.

771
01:27:39,170 --> 01:27:42,423
No, don't... No. No!

772
01:27:43,716 --> 01:27:45,301
Evy? Evy?

773
01:27:46,594 --> 01:27:50,640
RICK: No. No. Evy!

774
01:27:55,103 --> 01:27:56,896
Come back, Evy.

775
01:27:58,982 --> 01:28:00,900
Evy, come back.

776
01:28:02,068 --> 01:28:03,403
Come back.

777
01:28:51,617 --> 01:28:53,786
(BOTH SCREAMING)

778
01:29:14,432 --> 01:29:16,434
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

779
01:29:28,821 --> 01:29:30,198
Stay here.

780
01:29:41,542 --> 01:29:42,752
(GASPS)

781
01:29:44,003 --> 01:29:46,380
(SKITTERING)

782
01:30:22,291 --> 01:30:23,418
Whoa!

783
01:30:58,369 --> 01:31:00,413
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

784
01:31:05,084 --> 01:31:07,587
Try to think of it like this, 
Alex.

785
01:31:07,920 --> 01:31:10,173
She's gone to a better place.

786
01:31:10,339 --> 01:31:12,258
You know, 
like it says in the good book.

787
01:31:12,300 --> 01:31:13,926
The book. 
What?

788
01:31:14,010 --> 01:31:15,178
That's it.

789
01:31:15,261 --> 01:31:17,972
That's it. Come on, 
Uncle Jon! 
That's what?

790
01:31:18,055 --> 01:31:19,891
Come on! Come on! 
That's it! The book! 
What?

791
01:31:19,932 --> 01:31:21,684
(GRUNTING)

792
01:31:29,317 --> 01:31:33,279
You're too late, O'Connell. 
I have released 
the Army of Anubis.

793
01:31:34,030 --> 01:31:38,242
Lord Imhotep shall soon kill 
the Scorpion King 
and take command.

794
01:31:39,327 --> 01:31:40,828
Not after 
I get through with him.

795
01:31:47,501 --> 01:31:49,962
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

796
01:31:57,011 --> 01:31:58,095
<i>Niy!</i>

797
01:32:06,521 --> 01:32:09,106
<i>Niy! Niy!</i>

798
01:32:09,857 --> 01:32:11,275
You realize, of course,

799
01:32:11,359 --> 01:32:15,071
that this can only be done 
by someone who can actually 
read ancient Egyptian.

800
01:32:15,154 --> 01:32:18,115
I don't know about you, 
but I'm a tad rusty.

801
01:32:19,200 --> 01:32:20,576
Now where?

802
01:32:20,701 --> 01:32:23,037
We go right. 
How do you know?

803
01:32:24,038 --> 01:32:25,998
<i>"Kasheesh Osirian Nye."</i>

804
01:32:26,540 --> 01:32:29,585
Basically, "This way 
to the Scorpion King."

805
01:32:31,128 --> 01:32:32,672
Mum taught me.

806
01:32:35,967 --> 01:32:37,802
This just might work.

807
01:33:02,618 --> 01:33:04,245
(GROWLING)

808
01:33:06,789 --> 01:33:08,833
(JONATHAN CLEARING THROAT)

809
01:33:08,916 --> 01:33:11,210
It's time someone 
taught you a lesson, 
wench. Come on.

810
01:33:20,177 --> 01:33:22,096
This is for my sister.

811
01:33:24,974 --> 01:33:26,434
(GONG RINGING)

812
01:33:48,080 --> 01:33:49,498
(GRUNTING)

813
01:34:00,134 --> 01:34:01,510
(GRUNTING)

814
01:34:13,481 --> 01:34:15,316
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

815
01:34:47,181 --> 01:34:48,599
(GROWLING)

816
01:34:54,563 --> 01:34:57,066
(YELLING)

817
01:35:11,497 --> 01:35:13,416
Is that all you've got?

818
01:35:20,673 --> 01:35:23,050
(SHOUTING)

819
01:35:23,092 --> 01:35:25,010
(ALL YELLING)

820
01:36:05,342 --> 01:36:06,886
Hurry up, Alex!

821
01:36:07,136 --> 01:36:11,640
<i>"Hootash naraba oos Veesloo.</i>

822
01:36:12,141 --> 01:36:15,186
<i>"Ahm kum Ra. Ahm kum Dei."</i>

823
01:36:58,145 --> 01:37:01,398
<i>"Efday Shokran... 
Efday Shokran..."</i>

824
01:37:01,482 --> 01:37:04,276
Uncle Jon, I don't know 
what this last symbol is!

825
01:37:04,485 --> 01:37:07,863
What's it look like? 
It's a bird! A stork!

826
01:37:10,533 --> 01:37:12,993
I know that one! 
I know that one!

827
01:37:13,577 --> 01:37:15,204
Then what is it?

828
01:37:17,498 --> 01:37:18,916
<i>Ahmenophus!</i>

829
01:37:20,000 --> 01:37:23,254
That's it! 
<i>"Efday Shokran Ahmenophus!"</i>

830
01:38:04,378 --> 01:38:07,339
Why don't you pick on 
somebody your own size?

831
01:38:07,673 --> 01:38:10,467
Oh, my God. Evy! 
Take Alex.

832
01:38:10,551 --> 01:38:12,386
Go and help Rick. 
But Mom...

833
01:38:12,428 --> 01:38:13,596
No "buts," Alex.

834
01:38:13,679 --> 01:38:15,889
Come on, Alex. 
But... But...

835
01:38:17,725 --> 01:38:19,435
I'll be just fine.

836
01:38:19,727 --> 01:38:21,645
We did it, Uncle Jon! 
We did it!

837
01:38:21,729 --> 01:38:23,731
Right, partner. 
Now, let's go help your dad.

838
01:39:18,494 --> 01:39:20,245
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

839
01:39:32,299 --> 01:39:33,717
(GROWLING)

840
01:40:00,285 --> 01:40:01,662
Nefertiri.

841
01:40:03,163 --> 01:40:04,665
Anck-su-namun.

842
01:40:05,332 --> 01:40:07,000
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

843
01:40:26,186 --> 01:40:28,230
That's a little 
something new!

844
01:40:53,464 --> 01:40:55,549
(ALL CHEERING)

845
01:41:15,778 --> 01:41:17,237
(ALL SHOUTING)

846
01:41:31,460 --> 01:41:33,170
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

847
01:42:00,656 --> 01:42:02,658
Okay, now I'm a believer.

848
01:42:03,659 --> 01:42:04,785
Rick!

849
01:42:06,829 --> 01:42:08,455
Jonathan! 
Dad!

850
01:42:08,956 --> 01:42:10,124
It's a spear!

851
01:42:10,165 --> 01:42:12,835
The gold stick thing... 
It's a... It's a spear!

852
01:42:12,918 --> 01:42:15,796
Really? 
Doesn't look like a spear!

853
01:42:15,879 --> 01:42:19,007
No! That's because 
it opens up into one!

854
01:42:19,091 --> 01:42:21,135
Yes? And? 
Jonathan!

855
01:42:21,176 --> 01:42:24,346
It opens up into a spear!

856
01:42:24,429 --> 01:42:26,431
(ROARING)

857
01:42:29,810 --> 01:42:31,520
(BOTH SCREAMING)

858
01:42:53,542 --> 01:42:55,502
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

859
01:42:55,544 --> 01:42:57,838
(ALL SHOUTING)

860
01:43:10,767 --> 01:43:13,687
Rick! 
Evy?

861
01:43:20,235 --> 01:43:22,696
Twist it! 
Pull! I tried it! Push!

862
01:43:25,199 --> 01:43:26,575
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

863
01:43:26,658 --> 01:43:28,285
Jonathan, quick!

864
01:43:42,257 --> 01:43:45,385
Jonathan, throw it! 
Kill the Scorpion King!

865
01:43:45,469 --> 01:43:47,554
Send his army back 
to the Underworld!

866
01:43:48,222 --> 01:43:50,515
Step aside, Alex. 
I'm a professional.

867
01:44:01,235 --> 01:44:02,903
(SNARLING)

868
01:44:05,572 --> 01:44:08,075
(SPEAKING ANCIENT EGYPTIAN)

869
01:44:10,410 --> 01:44:11,536
Rick!

870
01:44:19,461 --> 01:44:21,254
No!

871
01:44:40,732 --> 01:44:41,775
No!

872
01:44:43,110 --> 01:44:44,528
(GROWLING)

873
01:44:47,030 --> 01:44:48,532
<i>Niy!</i>

874
01:44:54,496 --> 01:44:57,916
Go to hell, and take 
your friends with you!

875
01:44:59,793 --> 01:45:01,294
(GROWLING)

876
01:45:20,814 --> 01:45:22,983
(ALL CHEERING)

877
01:45:54,014 --> 01:45:55,348
(GRUNTS)

878
01:46:02,564 --> 01:46:03,940
(GRUNTS)

879
01:46:12,032 --> 01:46:13,241
(GRUNTS)

880
01:46:14,451 --> 01:46:15,535
Dad!

881
01:46:33,512 --> 01:46:36,723
Evy, no! Get out of here!

882
01:46:37,015 --> 01:46:38,850
Just get out of here!

883
01:46:39,643 --> 01:46:40,727
No!

884
01:46:45,232 --> 01:46:46,316
Mom!

885
01:46:59,746 --> 01:47:00,831
Hang on, Rick!

886
01:47:04,751 --> 01:47:06,211
(SCREAMS)

887
01:47:11,299 --> 01:47:12,843
Anck-su-namun!

888
01:47:17,514 --> 01:47:20,600
No! 
Anck-su-namun!

889
01:47:25,021 --> 01:47:26,565
Anck-su-namun.

890
01:47:43,039 --> 01:47:44,624
(GROWLING)

891
01:47:48,545 --> 01:47:49,463
(RUMBLING)

892
01:47:51,965 --> 01:47:53,091
Whoa!

893
01:47:57,971 --> 01:47:59,431
Let's go up!

894
01:48:18,992 --> 01:48:21,244
This whole damn place 
is gonna get sucked up!

895
01:48:21,328 --> 01:48:22,996
Let's move up! Go!

896
01:48:36,343 --> 01:48:38,470
JONATHAN: Go, Alex! 
Come on! Come on!

897
01:48:49,022 --> 01:48:50,857
Rick, we're trapped!

898
01:48:58,365 --> 01:48:59,449
IZZY: Hey!

899
01:49:02,702 --> 01:49:05,580
Izzy! 
Come on! 
Get your butts moving!

900
01:49:05,664 --> 01:49:07,874
Hurry up! Hurry up! 
I haven't got all day!

901
01:49:12,295 --> 01:49:13,922
RICK: Go! You're next!

902
01:49:17,425 --> 01:49:19,052
Right.

903
01:49:35,902 --> 01:49:37,487
Izzy! Thank you!

904
01:49:39,030 --> 01:49:41,616
O'Connell, who the hell 
you been messin' with 
this time?

905
01:49:41,658 --> 01:49:43,451
Huh? 
Oh, you know, the usual.

906
01:49:43,493 --> 01:49:45,704
Mummies, pygmies,

907
01:49:46,454 --> 01:49:47,747
big bugs.

908
01:49:57,799 --> 01:49:59,676
(SPEAKING ARABIC)

909
01:50:08,268 --> 01:50:09,978
(HORSE NEIGHING)

910
01:50:16,985 --> 01:50:19,446
I thought 
I almost lost you there.

911
01:50:19,988 --> 01:50:21,906
For a moment there, you did.

912
01:50:23,199 --> 01:50:25,619
Would you like to know 
what heaven looks like?

913
01:50:27,078 --> 01:50:28,246
Later.

914
01:50:32,250 --> 01:50:34,044
BOTH: Oh, please!

915
01:50:34,377 --> 01:50:36,838
That's half mine, 
you know. 
What?

916
01:50:36,921 --> 01:50:39,341
That's half mine. 
I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

917
01:50:39,382 --> 01:50:42,510
What? You took my gold stick! 
I know you took my gold stick!

918
01:50:42,552 --> 01:50:46,765
I swear on the head 
of my wife, I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

919
01:50:46,848 --> 01:50:48,850
IZZY: You haven't... 
You ain't got a wife!

920
01:50:48,892 --> 01:50:51,436
JONATHAN: I don't have 
your gold stick either!

